    faq: [
      { q: "What do traits mean in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Traits are permanent modifiers that affect how brainrots behave and appear. Unlike mutations, they are obtained through events and can be stacked, while also adding visual effects such as unique auras and emojis above a brainrot’s head. </p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "What is the best trait in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>The best trait in Steal a Brainrot is Strawberry, which offers a 9x multiplier and typically appears during Admin Abuse events.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "What is the rarest trait in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>The rarest traits are typically Admin Abuse exclusives like Strawberry, Meowl or the latest John Pork. These appear extremely rarely and may not be available again for weeks or even months.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Can you stack multiple traits on one Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Yes, multiple traits stack additively on a single brainrot regardless of rarity. The formula adds each trait's multiplier to your base income plus mutation modifier, so stacking rarer traits creates exponentially more value than spreading them across multiple brainrots.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "How does Sleepy trait affect my income?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Sleepy cuts your total income in half after all other calculations are applied. This makes it the worst trait in Steal a Brainrot, as it significantly lowers the value of even high-tier brainrots with the best traits or mutations. </p>\n                                        </div>" },
    ],
