    faq: [
      { q: "What are the rarest brainrots in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>OG tier brainrots like Meowl, original Strawberry Elephant and newly introduced Spyder Elephant are the absolute rarest.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "How many brainrots are in Steal a Brainrot right now?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Steal a Brainrot currently has 590+ brainrots, and the total keeps increasing with new Saturday updates. Up to 15 brainrots can drop in a single update.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "What are the rarity tiers in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>The main rarity tiers are Common, Rare, Epic, Legendary, Mythic, Brainrot God, Secret, and OG. Higher tiers are harder to find, cost more, and earn much more cash per second.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Which brainrots make the most money in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>At the top end, OG brainrots generate the highest base income, with Spyder Elephant generating $1B/s.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "What does exist count mean in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Exist count is the known total number of a specific brainrot that exists in the game. It matters because low-count brainrots are usually harder to get and more valuable in trades.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Which brainrots have the lowest known exist count?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Headless Horseman has one of the lowest known exist counts at around 54, while other ultra-low-count brainrots like Signore Carapace, Love Love Bear, and Strawberry Elephant are also highly scarce.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "How to get rare brainrots in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Players get rare brainrots through conveyor purchases, stealing from other players, Admin Abuse events, fusing/crafting, opening the Advent Calendar, spinning the wheel, and Lucky Blocks. </p>\n<p>For the rarest brainrots, Admin Abuse events and player-to-player trading are often more realistic than waiting for a natural spawn.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Can I transfer my brainrot collection to another account?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Yes, create a secondary account, meet yourself in-game on a private server, and steal your own brainrots. Keep your best brainrots safe from thieves on a secondary acoount. Go public with your main account only</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Are there legitimate marketplaces for buying Steal a Brainrot accounts and items?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Yes, marketplaces like Eldorado.gg specialize in secure in-game item and account trading. Escrow protection for your money, verified sellers, and 24/7 support should put you at ease. Avoid offers from social media to prevent scams.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "How do I safely trade or sell accounts with rare brainrots?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Use platforms with verified sellers and escrow protection that hold payment until both parties confirm the trade is completed.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Do brainrot spawn rates change by rarity?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Yes. Spawn rates drop sharply as rarity increases. Common brainrots spawn frequently, while Secret and OG odds become microscopic, which is a major reason top-tier brainrots are so valuable.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Can you complete the full brainrot index in Steal a Brainrot?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>You can work toward full index completion, but it is very difficult because some brainrots are limited-time, event-exclusive, or legacy-only. The game still marks a brainrot as collected once you have owned it at least once.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Are new brainrots added in updates?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>Yes. New brainrots are added through Saturday updates, including seasonal releases and collaborations, so any “full list” needs to be refreshed regularly.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "Are all brainrots obtainable from normal spawning?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>No. While many brainrots come from the conveyor belt or standard gameplay loops, some are tied to events, Lucky Blocks, Admin Abuse, or limited-time releases, so not every brainrot is realistically obtainable through normal spawning alone. </p>\n                                        </div>" },
      { q: "What are the newest brainrots currently in the game?", aHtml: "<div class=\"entry\">\n                                            <p>The newest brainrots were introduced in update 73: Spooky Kart, Jacko Jakat, Scorpi Inferni, Scarino Crowino, Puppetmaster.</p>\n                                        </div>" },
    ],
